{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01RU:statement", "parent_tag": "01RR", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The <TEXTITOPEN_0001>ring of rational functions on <MATH_0002><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nis the ring <MATH_0003> whose elements are rational functions with\naddition and multiplication as just described.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0003": "$R(X)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-ring-of-rational-functions}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:067f917cc2c51a216fcea6a8bc6cce9c31d91ef7d19d60b2228738e6d9a0a99a", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:016839c0fa5c1fa593566b8f69cacb8a2249a55ef19984411975e7ce477a6ca5", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0adf93503c4ca840d7376521a85e460941c0bbfd0165eba058eb6fd87eb5f24b"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01RR:prose-0004", "parent_tag": "01RR", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nFor schemes with finitely many irreducible components we can compute this.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:6eea996c31caa6cf3d42e407099a2ca810e958c6a598418fb1882bce319c4792", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6edef0c9a3a9f1d978b29478384d715a5ccc540c284f95f6709654a25069e107", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01RV:statement", "parent_tag": "01RR", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme with finitely many irreducible components\n<MATH_0002>. If <MATH_0003> is the generic point, then\n<MATH_0004>\nIf <MATH_0005> is reduced this is equal to <MATH_0006>.\nIf <MATH_0007> is integral then <MATH_0008>\nis a field.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X_1, \\ldots, X_n$", "MATH_0003": "$\\eta_i \\in X_i$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nR(X) = \\mathcal{O}_{X, \\eta_1} \\times \\ldots \\times \\mathcal{O}_{X, \\eta_n}\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\prod \\kappa(\\eta_i)$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$R(X) = \\mathcal{O}_{X, \\eta} = \\kappa(\\eta)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-integral-scheme-rational-functions}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:a2acdf7e4f060d2afae08b72ad6394ffeb307cabc1585571e91052051f71c774", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2d3b7696a5e83e37209bcb3ad45d57f4fc14508d2d52c1e1765ce9b16f7bc09b", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ca0e62891ce61a43fc365bd719f4e5a53ddb10002054ab6317611901f8cfd815"}
